Author: Van Tran <940988+vantt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Jul 17 10:34:25 2026 +0700

    feat(human-rounds-1): anti-loop gate resets on the item's own last human intervention
    
    The runner's anti-loop gate previously counted an item's lifetime visits
    (machine and human re-dispatches alike), so a human's reject-with-reason
    or answer had no effect on the budget: an item could stay stuck at the
    cap forever even after a person intervened.
    
    visitsSinceLastHumanEvent(events, id) counts doing-entries only since the
    item's own last human-attributed answer or reason-carrying move (actor
    'human') — the runner's own reason-carrying parks never qualify. The
    shipped lifetime visitCount metric and its call sites are unchanged.

